<article class="env-definition" id="01OB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01OB">Definition <span data-tag="01OB">27.21.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\mathcal{E}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ S$-module<a class="footnotemark" href="#a0000618191" id="a0000618191-mark"><sup>1</sup></a>. We denote </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \pi : \mathbf{P}(\mathcal{E}) = \underline{\text{Proj}}_ S(\text{Sym}(\mathcal{E})) \longrightarrow S  \]
</div>
  <p> and we call it the <em>projective bundle associated to $\mathcal{E}$</em>. The symbol $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbf{P}(\mathcal{E})}(n)$ indicates the invertible $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbf{P}(\mathcal{E})}$-module of Lemma <a href="/tag/01O4" data-tag="01O4">27.16.11</a> and is called the $n$th <em>twist of the structure sheaf</em>. </p>
</article>